      "status": "estimate",
      "isotopologue": "229Th19F+",
      "convention": null,
      "note": "Transferred unchanged from 232Th19F+ to 229Th19F+; not measured for the target isotope and not mass-scaled. Source-isotope uncertainty: 0.05 MHz; target-isotope transfer uncertainty is unquantified. "
    },
    "A_par": {
      "value": -20.1,
      "unit": "MHz",
      "uncertainty": null,
      "source": "Ng 2022 Table I p.5",
      "status": "estimate",
      "isotopologue": "229Th19F+",
      "convention": null,
      "note": "Transferred unchanged from 232Th19F+ to 229Th19F+; not measured for the target isotope and not mass-scaled. Source-isotope uncertainty: 0.1 MHz; target-isotope transfer uncertainty is unquantified. may absorb 2 c_I .. 6 c_I ~ 40-120 kHz of unmodelled nuclear spin-rotation -- [HAM] S2.6, OPEN-6"
    },
    "c_I": {
      "value": 20.0,
      "unit": "kHz",
      "uncertainty": null,
      "source": "[HAM] S2.6: B&C Table 8.12 c2(19F, CsF) = 15.1 kHz at B_v = 0.183782 cm-1, scaled linearly in B",
      "status": "estimate",
      "isotopologue": null,
      "convention": null,
      "note": "Order-of-magnitude analogy only. The 15.1 kHz CsF anchor gives 19.94 kHz after B scaling; neither the ThF+ sign nor a factor-of-three error bound is established. CsF is closed-shell; ThF+ is open-shell. B&C printed p.421/PDF p.453 discusses opposite-sign first/second-order contributions. Sweep this parameter rather than treating 20 kHz as a precision prediction"
    },
    "d_mf": {
      "value": 3.37,
      "unit": "D",
      "uncertainty": null,
      "source": "Ng 2022 Table I p.5",
      "status": "estimate",
      "isotopologue": "229Th19F+",
      "convention": "center_of_mass",
      "note": "Transferred unchanged from 232Th19F+ to 229Th19F+; not measured for the target isotope and not mass-scaled. Source-isotope uncertainty: 0.09 D; target-isotope transfer uncertainty is unquantified. ORIGIN-DEPENDENT for an ion: 2.74 D w.r.t. the Th nucleus (Skripnikov & Titov 2015 Table II) = 3.46 D at c.m."
    },
    "G_zz": {
      "value": 0.046532,
      "unit": "",
      "uncertainty": null,
      "source": "Ng thesis p.87 (0.048(2) for g_F < 0) as the measured sum: G_zz = 0.04756 - G_perp, which keeps |g_F=3/2| = 0.0149 (Ng 2022) exact -- [HAM] S3",
      "status": "estimate",
      "isotopologue": "229Th19F+",
      "convention": null,
      "note": "Transferred unchanged from 232Th19F+ to 229Th19F+; not measured for the target isotope and not mass-scaled. Source-isotope uncertainty: 0.002 ; target-isotope transfer uncertainty is unquantified. G_zz IS Ng's G_par. sign of g_F is NOT measured; theory forces g_F < 0. OPEN-4. The datum constrains G_zz + G_perp only, so the split between this value and G_xx/G_yy is Petrov's, not measured; the 0.6 % difference from the old G_par = 0.04756 sits well inside the +-0.002"
    },
    "G_xx": {
      "value": 0.00082211,
      "unit": "",
      "uncertainty": null,
      "source": "G_perp + G_Delta with G_perp = 1.02769e-3 and G_Delta = -2.0558e-4 from the second-order sums of Petrov & Skripnikov arXiv:2503.02840 Eqs. (3)-(15); docs/lit/lookup-effective-zeeman-tensor.md S2, S4",
      "status": "estimate",
      "isotopologue": "229Th19F+",
      "convention": null,
      "note": "Transferred unchanged from 232Th19F+ to 229Th19F+; not measured for the target isotope and not mass-scaled. Source-isotope uncertainty: none quantified; target-isotope transfer uncertainty is unquantified. ESTIMATE, not a measurement: second-order perturbation theory, ~20 % on G_Delta. G_Delta = (G_xx - G_yy)/2 < 0 is the parity-dependent part; it ADDS to the e level's g-factor, the component that mixes with the Omega = 0+ states (1Sigma+, 3Pi_0+). OPEN-10"
    },
    "G_yy": {
      "value": 0.00123327,
      "unit": "",
      "uncertainty": null,
      "source": "G_perp - G_Delta with G_perp = 1.02769e-3 and G_Delta = -2.0558e-4 from the second-order sums of Petrov & Skripnikov arXiv:2503.02840 Eqs. (3)-(15); docs/lit/lookup-effective-zeeman-tensor.md S2, S4",
      "status": "estimate",
      "isotopologue": "229Th19F+",
      "convention": null,
      "note": "Transferred unchanged from 232Th19F+ to 229Th19F+; not measured for the target isotope and not mass-scaled. Source-isotope uncertainty: none quantified; target-isotope transfer uncertainty is unquantified. ESTIMATE, not a measurement: second-order perturbation theory, ~20 % on G_Delta. See G_xx"
    },
